            <profile id="437a-27ac-07a1-238f" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The General rides a horse and has a hand weapon, heavy armour and shield. Army General. May have composite bow (+4) and thrusting spear (+3). May have partial plate armour (+1), half barding (+2) or cloth barding (+3), and may upgrade to warhorse (+7). Alternatively, may dismount with two handed weapon (-6). An Albanian General may have may have the Stratagem rule (+20). After 1440 Serbian and Albanian Generals may have full plate armour (+2), barding (+4) and lance (+6).</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f935-a63e-9569-45b8" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
